#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:3
msgid "Database Migrations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:5
msgid ""
"Migrations are a convenient way for you to alter your database in a "
"structured and organized manner. You could edit fragments of SQL by hand "
"but you would then be responsible for telling other developers that they "
"need to go and run them. You would also have to keep track of which "
"changes need to be run against the production machines next time you "
"deploy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:11
msgid ""
"The database table **migrations** tracks which migrations have already "
"been run, so all you have to do is make sure your migrations are in place"
" and run the ``spark migrate`` command to bring the database up to the "
"most recent state. You can also use ``spark migrate --all`` to include "
"migrations from all namespaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:23
msgid "Migration File Names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:25
msgid ""
"A migration file name is made up of a timestamp prefix, an underscore "
"(``_``), and a descriptive name (classname)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:28
msgid "2024-09-08-013653_AddBlogTable.php"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:30
msgid ""
"Each migration is numbered using the timestamp (**2024-09-08-013653**) "
"when the migration was created, in **YYYY-MM-DD-HHIISS** format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:33
msgid ""
"The descriptive name (**AddBlogTable**) for the migration is a classname "
"in PHP. So you must name a valid classname."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:36
msgid ""
"The year, month, day, and time in a prefix can be separated from each "
"other by dashes (``-``), underscores (``_``), or not at all. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:39
msgid "2012-10-31-100538_AlterBlogTrackViews.php"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:40
msgid "2012_10_31_100539_AlterBlogAddTranslations.php"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:41
msgid "20121031100537_AddBlog.php"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:43
msgid ""
"Each Migration is run in numeric order forward or backwards depending on "
"the method taken. This helps prevent numbering conflicts when working in "
"a team environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:49
msgid "Create a Migration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:51
msgid ""
"This will be the first migration for a new site which has a blog. All "
"migrations go in the **app/Database/Migrations/** directory and have "
"names such as **2022-01-31-013057_AddBlog.php**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:57
msgid ""
"The database connection and the database Forge class are both available "
"to you through ``$this->db`` and ``$this->forge``, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:60
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can use a command-line call to generate a skeleton "
"migration file. See `make:migration`_ in :ref:`command-line-tools` for "
"more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:63
msgid ""
"Since the migration class is a PHP class, the classname must be unique in"
" every migration file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:66
msgid "Foreign Keys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:68
msgid ""
"When your tables include Foreign Keys, migrations can often cause "
"problems as you attempt to drop tables and columns. To temporarily bypass"
" the foreign key checks while running migrations, use the "
"``disableForeignKeyChecks()`` and ``enableForeignKeyChecks()`` methods on"
" the database connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:75
msgid "Database Groups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:77
msgid ""
"A migration will only be run against a single database group. If you have"
" multiple groups defined in **app/Config/Database.php**, then by default "
"it will run against the ``$defaultGroup`` as specified in that same "
"configuration file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:81
msgid ""
"There may be times when you need different schemas for different database"
" groups. Perhaps you have one database that is used for all general site "
"information, while another database is used for mission critical data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:85
msgid ""
"You can ensure that migrations are run only against the proper group by "
"setting the ``$DBGroup`` property on your migration. This name must match"
" the name of the database group exactly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:91
msgid ""
"The **migrations** table that tracks which migrations have already been "
"run will be always created in the default database group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:95
msgid "Namespaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:97
msgid ""
"The migration library can automatically scan all namespaces you have "
"defined within **app/Config/Autoload.php** or loaded from an external "
"source like Composer, using the ``$psr4`` property for matching directory"
" names. It will include all migrations it finds in "
"**Database/Migrations**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:102
msgid ""
"Each namespace has its own version sequence, this will help you upgrade "
"and downgrade each module (namespace) without affecting other namespaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:104
msgid ""
"For example, assume that we have the following namespaces defined in our "
"Autoload configuration file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:110
msgid ""
"This will look for any migrations located at both "
"**APPPATH/Database/Migrations** and "
"**ROOTPATH/MyCompany/Database/Migrations**. This makes it simple to "
"include migrations in your re-usable, modular code suites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:118
msgid "Command-Line Tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/dbmgmt/migration.rst:120
msgid ""
"CodeIgniter ships with several :doc:`commands </cli/spark_commands>` that"
" are available from the command line to help you work with migrations. "
"These tools make things easier for those of you that wish to use them. "
"The tools primarily provide access to the same methods that are available"
" within the MigrationRunner class."
msgstr ""

